WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.870
In 1932, the Sukkur Barrage opened
across the River Indus in Pakistan.

2
00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.910
Today, 23 barrages divert it into canals:

3
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.110
the largest contiguous surface water
irrigation system in the world,

4
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:15.470
says the World Bank.

5
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.210
About 129 cubic kilometres of
Indus water are taken each year,

6
00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:22.770
for irrigation and other uses.

7
00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:28.010
Yet salt now threatens farming on up
to 43 per cent of the irrigated area.

8
00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.230
Where is that salt coming from?

9
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:31.630
Too much fertiliser?

10
00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:32.690
Sea water?

11
00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:35.150
Or was the soil always salty?

12
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.790
In this mission, you'll trace
the water from dam to barrage,

13
00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:40.470
canal and field.

14
00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:43.110
Then you'll weigh its advantages
against its disadvantages,

15
00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:46.210
and judge which outweighs the other.

16
00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:51.410
Your mission: explain why salt is
spoiling Pakistan's irrigated fields.
